+## Proposed native Alert
+
+Immutable source: [Alert wrapper](https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui/blob/d75a96ab781f3d659be1ad287347d5887ce9f2fc/apps/v4/registry/bases/base/ui/alert.tsx), [complete examples](https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui/blob/d75a96ab781f3d659be1ad287347d5887ce9f2fc/apps/v4/registry/bases/base/examples/alert-example.tsx), and Nova lines 19–42. See [Alert contract](alert.md), [hash manifest](../tests/reference/alert-sources.json) and proposed [draft PR21](https://github.com/sveltery/ui/pull/21). Alert-local work starts at landed Label main `b7d5ed09ebc6530adc57be1d85cfa8a4680ea3c2`; this exact shared patch must be reconciled after PR19 and PR20 integrate. Existing records and dependency pins are retained.
+
+| Adaptation/source | Observable pinned React versus local behavior | Rationale, evidence and decision status |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Native div framework API; wrapper above | React className, children, style objects, refs and synthetic events become Svelte class, snippets, CSS strings, undefined/null bindable native div refs/symbol attachments and native events. All four parts remain divs; root role/data-slot and caller class precedence remain pinned. Named native props types are added as Svelte conveniences; the private CVA helper stays private. | Idiomatic supported Svelte integration; paired [DOM](../tests/dom/alert.test.ts), [SSR](../scripts/check-alert-ssr.mjs), [types](../tests/alert-types.ts), [browser](../tests/browser/alert.spec.ts) and [fresh consumers](../tests/installation/alert.spec.ts). Proposed and unlanded. Existing recorded framework-substitution acceptance covers class/snippets/refs/attachments/native events/CSS where exposed; no additional Alert-specific or named-type acceptance decision is recorded. Framework assertions earn no React parity credit. |
+| Basic Example/ExampleWrapper scaffold; examples above | The actual Basic body runs under native sections/headings in local and paired galleries. The three Alert compositions retain text/classes/parts; upstream scaffold layout/APIs remain unimplemented. | Keep the dependency-available bounded example. [Exact-function provenance](../scripts/tests/alert-provenance.test.mjs) and paired browser probes. Proposed; separate scaffold acceptance not recorded. |
+| Nova and theme scaffold; Nova lines above | The upstream `.style-nova` scope becomes the existing repository component layer; both paired harnesses use current consumer light tokens and supplemental dark-class witnesses. Full upstream stylesheet scope/theme packaging and dark palettes are unimplemented. | Existing Nova packaging, exact source bytes and paired computed style probes. Proposed; separate stylesheet/theme scaffold acceptance is not recorded. |
+| With Icons, Destructive and With Actions examples | These actual function bodies require missing configurable IconPlaceholder and/or Badge. They remain unimplemented; destructive/action/inline-SVG/link selector probes are supplemental native tests only. | Explicit deferred scope; no substituted gallery or full parity claim. |
+
+No dedicated upstream Alert tests are claimed or ported. Source-derived local assertions and passing proposed-snapshot checks certify only the exercised behavior. Final integration, final-head secured CI and independent/configured automatic reviews remain blocked until pending checkpoints serialize; full gallery/library parity and production readiness remain blocked.
